WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER, AND CANNOT

  The CrisisMMD v2.0 corpus itself is NOT redistributed here and is NOT covered by
  this licence. What this package ships is derived from it: eight- and
  ten-component reductions of CLIP embeddings, byte counts, labels, hazard tags and
  recovered arrival times. The posts and images themselves are not included.

  CrisisMMD is obtained from its authors at
  https://crisisnlp.qcri.org/data/crisismmd/ under their terms, and onward use of
  anything derived from it remains subject to those terms and to the platform terms
  governing the original posts, in addition to this licence. If those terms and this
  licence conflict for some use, the corpus authors' terms govern that use.

  data/traces/ contains summary statistics and provenance for measured LTE capacity
  traces published by the Mahimahi project; the traces themselves are third-party
  material under their own terms, recorded in data/traces/provenance.json.
